\ by-rfl (plan FE1g-4; docs/design/FE1G_TACTICS.md 2.4 and 5.3).
\ Lean: theorem refl_p (p : Prop) : p = p := by rfl
\ gives fun (p : Prop) => @Eq.refl.{1} Prop p. Natural LeanForth cannot
\ write Prop yet (plan FE2). Without the library's elaboration data the
\ text stops at end with error 139, exit 2; with it (--elab-data) by-rfl
\ stops with error 97, exit 4, Lean's own message for 0 + n = n (pinned
\ Lean's rfl fails there too: 0 + n does not reduce to n).
\ tests/front/tactic-basic.fs runs it with a stand-in that gives the
\ statement forall (p : Prop), p = p (whatever the words below say); the
\ kernel accepts it.
theorem refl_p
  Nat explicit: n
  0 n + n =
:= by
  by-rfl
end refl_p
